  "district": "8th Congressional District",
  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "Tennessee's 8th Congressional District was significantly redrawn in May 2026 to include more of Shelby County (Memphis) and lose several counties to the reconfigured 5th and 9th Districts. Incumbent Republican David Kustoff is seeking a sixth term in a district that was made more geographically compact but still leans heavily Republican, with Cook Political Report rating it 'Solid R.' Four Democrats are competing in the August 6 Democratic primary to challenge Kustoff in the November general election, alongside six independent candidates. The redrawn map has been controversial, with opponents arguing it dilutes urban Black Democratic voting strength in Memphis, while supporters say it modernizes the redistricting process by removing racial data from mapmaking.",
  "polling": [],
  "polling_note": "No independent opinion polls were found for this specific race as of June 2026. Cook Political Report rates the race as 'Solid R.'",
